{"externally_confirmed_facts":["`java.security.spec.X509EncodedKeySpec` is a transparent key-specification class for an ASN.1 `SubjectPublicKeyInfo` encoding of a public key. Its documented format name is `"X.509"`; it is not documented as an X.509 certificate or certificate-path object.","The one-argument constructor, `X509EncodedKeySpec(byte[] encodedKey)`, accepts a public key assumed to be encoded according to the X.509 standard. It copies the supplied array, throws `NullPointerException` for a null array, and `getEncoded()` returns the X.509 encoding in a new array.","The two-argument constructor accepts encoded key material and an algorithm name. It is documented as useful when later consumers may not know the key algorithm; it rejects null inputs and an empty algorithm string. This overload is available since Java 9.","`KeyFactory` is the documented API for conversion between opaque `Key` objects and transparent `KeySpec` representations. `KeyFactory.generatePublic(KeySpec)` produces a `PublicKey` from an appropriate specification and throws `InvalidKeySpecException` if the specification is inappropriate for that key factory.","Neither the reviewed Oracle `X509EncodedKeySpec`, `KeyFactory`, nor `Key` documentation defines an operation, state, or API event named `preparedKeyMaterial` or “preparation of the encoded key material.” The official documentation therefore supplies no prescribed remediation for that rule-local predicate.","The rule source scopes itself to `java.security.spec.X509EncodedKeySpec`. Its exact relevant text is:
```
SPEC java.security.spec.X509EncodedKeySpec

OBJECTS
    byte[] encodedKey;

EVENTS
    c1: X509EncodedKeySpec(encodedKey);
    Con := c1;
```
Thus, as stated by the rule text, its event is constructor-shaped, has one `byte[]` argument named `encodedKey`, and is not an ordinary method-call event with an instance receiver.","The rule’s exact requirement and postcondition are:
```
REQUIRES
    preparedKeyMaterial[encodedKey];

ENSURES
    speccedKey[this, _] after Con;
```
The source contains no definition, producer, or runtime test for `preparedKeyMaterial`; it does not state a condition involving an algorithm, key size, trust anchor, certificate chain, provenance, or subsequent use.","The supplied rule text has no `CONSTRAINTS` section and declares only `X509EncodedKeySpec(encodedKey)`. On the text of the rule, it does not match a method merely because that method shares the API class’s name: the rule is scoped by `SPEC java.security.spec.X509EncodedKeySpec` and declares only that one-argument constructor-shaped event. The rule file does not document an analyzer’s actual type-, overload-, or call-resolution behavior.","The Java `Key` documentation describes encoded keys as external encoded forms for use outside the JVM, including transmission to another party. It identifies X.509 `SubjectPublicKeyInfo` as the ASN.1 public-key format associated with the name `"X.509"`. Consequently, `X509EncodedKeySpec` has a documented representation contract for persisted or wire key material.","The reviewed documentation does not provide a general byte-for-byte persistence guarantee, a wire-format migration procedure, or a conversion mapping from X.509 `SubjectPublicKeyInfo` to unrelated key containers or certificate encodings. It also provides no migration path specifically for changing construction or satisfying `preparedKeyMaterial`.","`X509EncodedKeySpec` and its one-argument constructor are documented since Java 1.2. The `(byte[], String)` overload is documented since Java 9. Provider acceptance remains dependent on the selected `KeyFactory`; the API permits `InvalidKeySpecException` when the supplied specification is inappropriate."],"sources":[{"relevance":"Official Java API specification for the governed class, its X.509 SubjectPublicKeyInfo representation, constructors, copying behavior, format name, and version annotations.","limitations":"Does not define the Crypto-API-Rules predicate `preparedKeyMaterial` and does not prescribe remediation for that predicate.","claim":"Documents `X509EncodedKeySpec` as an X.509 SubjectPublicKeyInfo public-key encoding and documents constructor/getEncoded semantics.","authority":"official","url":"https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/security/spec/X509EncodedKeySpec.html"},{"relevance":"Official Java API specification for the documented conversion from KeySpec to PublicKey and provider-dependent invalid-specification failure.","limitations":"Does not define a migration procedure for persisted application data or the rule-local preparation predicate.","claim":"Documents `KeyFactory.generatePublic(KeySpec)` and `InvalidKeySpecException` for an inappropriate specification.","authority":"official","url":"https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/security/KeyFactory.html"},{"relevance":"Official Java API specification for the meaning of an encoded key as an external representation, including the X.509 SubjectPublicKeyInfo public-key format.","limitations":"Does not guarantee byte-for-byte persistence compatibility or define migrations to other containers.","claim":"Documents encoded key forms for external use and associates public-key X.509 encoding with SubjectPublicKeyInfo.","authority":"official","url":"https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/security/Key.html"},{"relevance":"Official historical Java API documentation supporting Java 8 availability of the class and one-argument constructor.","limitations":"Does not cover the Java-9-added algorithm overload or define the rule-local predicate.","claim":"Documents the class and one-argument constructor in Java SE 8.","authority":"official","url":"https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/security/spec/X509EncodedKeySpec.html"},{"relevance":"Primary source for the exact CrySL rule scope, declared event, argument declaration, predicate requirement, and postcondition.","limitations":"Does not define `preparedKeyMaterial`, identify predicate producers, establish runtime truth of the predicate, or document analyzer type/overload/call-graph resolution.","claim":"States `SPEC java.security.spec.X509EncodedKeySpec`, the one-argument constructor-shaped event, `REQUIRES preparedKeyMaterial[encodedKey]`, and the `speccedKey` postcondition.","authority":"primary","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CROSSINGTUD/Crypto-API-Rules/refs/heads/master/JavaCryptographicArchitecture/src/X509EncodedKeySpec.crysl"}],"queries_performed":["Reviewed the official Oracle Java SE 25 API documentation for `java.security.spec.X509EncodedKeySpec`: https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/security/spec/X509EncodedKeySpec.html","Reviewed the official Oracle Java SE 25 API documentation for `java.security.KeyFactory`: https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/security/KeyFactory.html","Reviewed the official Oracle Java SE 25 API documentation for `java.security.Key`: https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/security/Key.html","Reviewed the official Oracle Java SE 8 API documentation for `java.security.spec.X509EncodedKeySpec`: https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/security/spec/X509EncodedKeySpec.html","Reviewed the supplied primary CrySL rule source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CROSSINGTUD/Crypto-API-Rules/refs/heads/master/JavaCryptographicArchitecture/src/X509EncodedKeySpec.crysl"],"externally_unresolved_questions":["What operation or provenance condition causes `preparedKeyMaterial[encodedKey]` to hold is unresolved: the rule source declares the predicate but provides neither a definition nor producer rules.","Whether a particular detector correctly resolved a specific call target, overload, namesake type, reflection path, native boundary, deserialization boundary, or interprocedural data flow cannot be determined from the `.crysl` rule text.","Whether a particular selected security provider accepts a given algorithm and encoded key is unresolved without provider- and input-specific documentation or testing; the documented API permits `InvalidKeySpecException` for an inappropriate specification.","No official source reviewed specifies how existing persisted or wire data should migrate if its representation is changed, nor does one define a migration related to the rule-local `preparedKeyMaterial` predicate."]}
